# Requests to RimBank.Host. Run the AppHost (dotnet run --project src/RimBank.AppHost) and set @host to the
# rimbank-host URL and @keycloak to the keycloak URL shown in the Aspire dashboard.
@host = http://localhost:5100
@keycloak = http://localhost:8080

### Readiness: every health check must pass. The probes are the only anonymous endpoints (ADR 0019).
GET {{host}}/health

### Liveness: only checks tagged "live"
GET {{host}}/alive

### Authentication (ADR 0019): without a token, every other request is a 401 application/problem+json, even when no
# endpoint matches, so the host never reveals which routes exist:
# {
#   "type": "urn:rimbank:problem:shared:unauthenticated",
#   "title": "Unauthorized",
#   "status": 401,
#   "detail": "This operation needs a valid access token. Send one in the Authorization header as 'Bearer <token>'.",
#   "instance": "/PartyReferenceDataDirectory/does-not-exist/Retrieve",
#   "errorCode": "shared.unauthenticated",
#   "traceId": "<32 hex characters, the trace shown in the Aspire dashboard>"
# }
GET {{host}}/PartyReferenceDataDirectory/does-not-exist/Retrieve

### A token from the local Keycloak, with the dev-only client of src/RimBank.AppHost/Realms (client-credentials grant)
# @name token
POST {{keycloak}}/realms/rimbank/protocol/openid-connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=client_credentials&client_id=rimbank-dev-client&client_secret=rimbank-dev-client-secret-local-only

### Problem Details (ADR 0015): with a valid token, no endpoint matches, so the host answers 404
# application/problem+json with "type": "urn:rimbank:problem:shared:not-found" and "errorCode": "shared.not-found".
GET {{host}}/PartyReferenceDataDirectory/does-not-exist/Retrieve
Authorization: Bearer {{token.response.body.$.access_token}}

### Party Reference Data Directory (ADR 0024): register a party. The ETag of the answer is the entry's version, "1".
# @name register
POST {{host}}/PartyReferenceDataDirectory/Register
Authorization: Bearer {{token.response.body.$.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: {{$guid}}

{ "PartyType": "Person" }

### Update the entry (roadmap 1.8, ADR 0027): If-Match is the ETag you last read. Answers 200 with ETag "2" and the
# entry's RefreshDate. Without If-Match it is 428 shared.if-match-required.
PUT {{host}}/PartyReferenceDataDirectory/{{register.response.body.$.PartyReferenceDataDirectoryEntryId}}/Update
Authorization: Bearer {{token.response.body.$.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: {{$guid}}
If-Match: "1"

{ "PartyType": "Organisation" }

### The same Update again with a new key: "1" is no longer the current version, so it is 409 party.version-conflict.
PUT {{host}}/PartyReferenceDataDirectory/{{register.response.body.$.PartyReferenceDataDirectoryEntryId}}/Update
Authorization: Bearer {{token.response.body.$.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: {{$guid}}
If-Match: "1"

{ "PartyType": "Person" }

### Retrieve the entry: Organisation, its RefreshDate, and ETag "2".
GET {{host}}/PartyReferenceDataDirectory/{{register.response.body.$.PartyReferenceDataDirectoryEntryId}}/Retrieve
Authorization: Bearer {{token.response.body.$.access_token}}

### Reference BQ (roadmap 1.20, ADR 0032): record the party's declared legal standing and documents. If-Match is the
# entry's current version ("2" after the Update above). Answers 200 with ETag "3": PartyLegalStructure in BIAN spelling
# ("PrivateLimitedCompany"), CustomerSinceDate "2015-03-02", the description trimmed, the validity dates as YYYY-MM-DD.
PUT {{host}}/PartyReferenceDataDirectory/{{register.response.body.$.PartyReferenceDataDirectoryEntryId}}/Reference/{{register.response.body.$.ReferenceId}}/Update
Authorization: Bearer {{token.response.body.$.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: {{$guid}}
If-Match: "2"

{
  "PartyLegalStructure": "private limited company",
  "PoliticalExposureType": "Politicalexposuredomestic",
  "PoliticalExposureDescriptionRecord": " Member of a regional council since 2021 ",
  "CustomerSinceDate": "2015-03-02T10:00:00+01:00",
  "GovernmentIssuedDocumentDetails": {
    "PartyDocumentType": "PersonalDocument",
    "DocumentReference": {
      "DocumentIdentification": { "IdentifierValue": "23AB45678" },
      "DocumentName": "Passport",
      "DocumentValidityPeriod": {
        "FromDateTime": { "DateTimeContent": "2023-04-01" },
        "ToDateTime": { "DateTimeContent": "2033-03-31" }
      }
    }
  },
  "DocumentDirectoryEntryInstanceReference": { "DocumentDirectoryEntryIdentification": "DOC-000123" }
}

### Retrieve the Reference: the same values, ETag "3". Send If-None-Match: "3" to get 304 Not Modified.
GET {{host}}/PartyReferenceDataDirectory/{{register.response.body.$.PartyReferenceDataDirectoryEntryId}}/Reference/{{register.response.body.$.ReferenceId}}/Retrieve
Authorization: Bearer {{token.response.body.$.access_token}}

### A description without an exposure is refused on the resulting Reference: 400 application/problem+json with
# "errorCode": "party.reference-invalid" and errors["PoliticalExposureDescriptionRecord"]. Nothing is stored.
PUT {{host}}/PartyReferenceDataDirectory/{{register.response.body.$.PartyReferenceDataDirectoryEntryId}}/Reference/{{register.response.body.$.ReferenceId}}/Update
Authorization: Bearer {{token.response.body.$.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: {{$guid}}
If-Match: "3"

{ "PoliticalExposureType": "Nopoliticalexposure" }

### Associations BQ (roadmap 1.11, ADR 0033): register a second party, to associate with the first one.
# @name associate
POST {{host}}/PartyReferenceDataDirectory/Register
Authorization: Bearer {{token.response.body.$.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: {{$guid}}

{ "PartyType": "Person" }

### Associate them: "the first party is the parent of the second". Answers 200 with ETag "1" (the association's own
# version), AssociateType in BIAN spelling and FromDateTime "2024-01-01T00:00:00Z". The associate must be registered
# (422 party.associate-not-registered) and must not be the party itself (422 party.self-association).
# @name association
POST {{host}}/PartyReferenceDataDirectory/{{register.response.body.$.PartyReferenceDataDirectoryEntryId}}/Associations/Register
Authorization: Bearer {{token.response.body.$.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: {{$guid}}

{
  "AssociateReference": { "PartyReference": "{{associate.response.body.$.PartyReferenceDataDirectoryEntryId}}" },
  "AssociateType": "partyisparentofparty",
  "AssociationValidFromToDate": { "FromDateTime": "2024-01-01" }
}

### End the association: If-Match is the association's ETag. Answers 200 with ETag "2"; the type is kept.
PUT {{host}}/PartyReferenceDataDirectory/{{register.response.body.$.PartyReferenceDataDirectoryEntryId}}/Associations/{{association.response.body.$.AssociationsId}}/Update
Authorization: Bearer {{token.response.body.$.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: {{$guid}}
If-Match: "1"

{ "AssociationValidFromToDate": { "FromDateTime": "2024-01-01", "ToDateTime": "2025-12-31" } }

### Retrieve the association: the same values, ETag "2". Send If-None-Match: "2" to get 304 Not Modified. Only the
# owning entry finds it: the second party's id in the path is 404 party.association-not-found.
GET {{host}}/PartyReferenceDataDirectory/{{register.response.body.$.PartyReferenceDataDirectoryEntryId}}/Associations/{{association.response.body.$.AssociationsId}}/Retrieve
Authorization: Bearer {{token.response.body.$.access_token}}

### Reference BQ (roadmap 1.21, ADR 0034): register the group the first party (an organisation since its Update) belongs to.
# @name group
POST {{host}}/PartyReferenceDataDirectory/Register
Authorization: Bearer {{token.response.body.$.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: {{$guid}}

{ "PartyType": "Organisation" }

### Link the first party to its group (an organisation) and its officer (the second party, a person). Each reference is
# loaded on the write side: it must be registered (422 party.referenced-party-not-registered), not the party itself
# (422 party.self-reference), and of the right type (422 party.referenced-party-type-mismatch). Answers 200 with ETag
# "4", the role trimmed.
PUT {{host}}/PartyReferenceDataDirectory/{{register.response.body.$.PartyReferenceDataDirectoryEntryId}}/Reference/{{register.response.body.$.ReferenceId}}/Update
Authorization: Bearer {{token.response.body.$.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: {{$guid}}
If-Match: "3"

{
  "CorporateCustomerReference": { "PartyReference": "{{group.response.body.$.PartyReferenceDataDirectoryEntryId}}" },
  "CorporateCustomerLegalEntityReference": { "PartyReference": "{{group.response.body.$.PartyReferenceDataDirectoryEntryId}}" },
  "CompanyOfficerReference": { "PartyReference": "{{associate.response.body.$.PartyReferenceDataDirectoryEntryId}}" },
  "CompanyOfficerRole": " Director "
}

### The group as the officer: 422 application/problem+json, "errorCode": "party.referenced-party-type-mismatch", and a
# detail naming CompanyOfficerReference.PartyReference. Nothing is stored.
PUT {{host}}/PartyReferenceDataDirectory/{{register.response.body.$.PartyReferenceDataDirectoryEntryId}}/Reference/{{register.response.body.$.ReferenceId}}/Update
Authorization: Bearer {{token.response.body.$.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: {{$guid}}
If-Match: "4"

{ "CompanyOfficerReference": { "PartyReference": "{{group.response.body.$.PartyReferenceDataDirectoryEntryId}}" } }

### An organisation with corporate references cannot become a person: 422 party.corporate-references-need-organisation.
# Clear the four references first.
PUT {{host}}/PartyReferenceDataDirectory/{{register.response.body.$.PartyReferenceDataDirectoryEntryId}}/Update
Authorization: Bearer {{token.response.body.$.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: {{$guid}}
If-Match: "4"

{ "PartyType": "Person" }

### BankRelations BQ (roadmap 1.12, ADR 0035): the second party (a person) is the first party's relationship manager.
# The employee or unit is loaded on the write side, like a Reference reference. Answers 200 with ETag "5",
# BankRelationType "RelationshipManager" and RelationshipStartDate "2024-01-01T00:00:00Z".
PUT {{host}}/PartyReferenceDataDirectory/{{register.response.body.$.PartyReferenceDataDirectoryEntryId}}/BankRelations/{{register.response.body.$.BankRelationsId}}/Update
Authorization: Bearer {{token.response.body.$.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: {{$guid}}
If-Match: "4"

{
  "BankRelationType": "relationshipmanager",
  "BusinessUnitEmployeeReference": { "PartyReference": "{{associate.response.body.$.PartyReferenceDataDirectoryEntryId}}" },
  "BankRelationReference": {
    "RelationshipStartDate": { "DateTimeContent": "2024-01-01" },
    "RelationshipLifecycleStatus": { "StatusDescription": "Active" }
  }
}

### Retrieve the BankRelations: the same values, ETag "5". Send If-None-Match: "5" to get 304 Not Modified.
GET {{host}}/PartyReferenceDataDirectory/{{register.response.body.$.PartyReferenceDataDirectoryEntryId}}/BankRelations/{{register.response.body.$.BankRelationsId}}/Retrieve
Authorization: Bearer {{token.response.body.$.access_token}}

### A servicing branch must be an organisation, and the kept manager is a person: 422 application/problem+json,
# "errorCode": "party.referenced-party-type-mismatch", detail "BusinessUnitEmployeeReference.PartyReference must name a
# party of type Organisation.". Send the group's id as the reference too, and it is accepted.
PUT {{host}}/PartyReferenceDataDirectory/{{register.response.body.$.PartyReferenceDataDirectoryEntryId}}/BankRelations/{{register.response.body.$.BankRelationsId}}/Update
Authorization: Bearer {{token.response.body.$.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: {{$guid}}
If-Match: "5"

{ "BankRelationType": "ServicingBranch" }

### The party itself as its relationship manager: 422 party.self-reference. Nothing is stored.
PUT {{host}}/PartyReferenceDataDirectory/{{register.response.body.$.PartyReferenceDataDirectoryEntryId}}/BankRelations/{{register.response.body.$.BankRelationsId}}/Update
Authorization: Bearer {{token.response.body.$.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: {{$guid}}
If-Match: "5"

{ "BusinessUnitEmployeeReference": { "PartyReference": "{{register.response.body.$.PartyReferenceDataDirectoryEntryId}}" } }

### A BIAN part RimBank does not record: 400 party.bank-relations-field-not-supported with
# errors["BankRelationReference.RelationshipIdentification"]. Nothing is stored.
PUT {{host}}/PartyReferenceDataDirectory/{{register.response.body.$.PartyReferenceDataDirectoryEntryId}}/BankRelations/{{register.response.body.$.BankRelationsId}}/Update
Authorization: Bearer {{token.response.body.$.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: {{$guid}}
If-Match: "5"

{ "BankRelationReference": { "RelationshipIdentification": { "IdentifierValue": "REL-1" } } }
